          <caption>
            <p>Metatarsal Head Parabolas Depicting Brachymetatarsia. The dotted lines in the image illustrate the metatarsal head parabolas in a human foot with brachymetatarsia, highlighting the shortened fourth metatarsal. The "distance A" shown in the image represents the length that the metatarsus should be lengthened to restore the normal parabola. This distance must be at least 5 mm for a diagnosis of brachymetatarsia. Contributed by AO Sabry, MD</p>
